  }, {
    "id" : "feature-summary-h",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 2
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Summary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "a6f2e0a1",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Adds a new LegalEntity root entity (name, unique 20-character alphanumeric lei, draft/active/retired status) with its spec-time descriptor and default form shipped verbatim. An observer sheet serves the register and a selection query that excludes retired rows. The Legal entities screen is built from its mock and registered under Reference data, in three tasks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "feature-design-h",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 2
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Design"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "3d3ca404",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Grounding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "53447412",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "The spec names cdm.base.staticdata.party.LegalEntity as vocabulary only; it is not served in this deployment, so LegalEntity is a new root entity in the application module, using the spec's approved descriptor "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "entity_descriptors/cdm.base.staticdata.party.LegalEntity.json",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " verbatim."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "b009c59c",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "LegalEntity entity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "a89c35e3",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Root bean with three required fields: "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "name",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (text, the legal name), "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "lei",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (text) and "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "status",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (lifecycle draft | active | retired, default draft). "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "lei",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " is unique and must match 20 alphanumeric characters; both rules are enforced on save by the entity's validation. The status lifecycle yields a generated enum "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "LegalEntity.status",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "; it is not hand-written beside the entity. The observer sheet is the entity's only remote surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "966ed68c",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Retired entities (R1 / A1)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "c88ed9fb",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Retiring is a status change, never a delete: the row stays in the register. \"Selection for new business\" is the reference lookup of legal entities offered to other features. It is a query on the sheet that returns only non-retired rows (draft and active). The register screen itself uses the unfiltered query, so retired rows remain visible there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "c2f2a189",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Default form and screen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "ebaaaa9a",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "The default form "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "ui/cdm.base.staticdata.party.LegalEntity.js",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " is shipped verbatim beside the entity class. The \"Legal entities\" screen follows the mock "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "ui/legal-entities.screen.js",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " region for region: a filter bar (name, lei, status), a dense table (name, lei, status; open, delete), and a side panel showing the default form (save, cancel). Retired rows are visibly marked. It is registered under "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Reference data › Legal entities",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "."
    } ]
